Dependency vulnerability fix — opentelemetry-api 1.45.1 -> 1.45.2 (CVE-2026-126360 / GHSA-mf5v-w3w3-f6cg)
date: 2026-11-14 (UTC)   branch: m10/sec-otel-1452   base: main f57d22f8

## 1. How it was found
  CI job audit (required) failed on PR #368 (run 43529647138, job 132257933932) — not caused by that PR:
  "Found 1 known vulnerability in 1 package / opentelemetry-api 1.45.1 CVE-2026-126360 1.45.2"
  The advisory was published 2026-11-12T22:24Z (OSV), after the last green main run, so main is affected too.
  Advisory (OSV): quadratic-time regex backtracking in TraceContextTextMapPropagator.extract() on a malformed
  traceparent with an embedded newline (CWE-1333, DoS). opentelemetry-api is transitive (via fastapi); AGOS does not
  call the propagator itself.

## 2. Red — pip-audit -r requirements.lock on main (local, pip-audit in Python 3.11 venv)
  Found 1 known vulnerability in 1 package
